# Introduction to Inheritance

::: columns
:::: {.column width=50%}
::: {.block}
## Inheritance

Inheritance allows a new class to extend an existing class.  The
new class inherits the members of the class it extends.
:::
In the real world, many objects are specialized versions of more general objects

- Example: grasshoppers and bees are specialized types of insect
- In addition to the general insect characteristics, they have unique characteristics:
  - Grasshoppers can jump
  - Bees can sting, make honey, and build hives
::::
:::: {.column width=50%}
\begin{figure}
\includegraphics[scale=0.5]{figures/ch11-fig-11-1-insect-inheritance}
\label{fig:ch11-fig-11-1-insect-inheritance}
\caption{Bumblebees and grasshoppers are specialized versions of an insect \parencite[pg.606]{gaddis-2021}}
\end{figure}
::::
:::

# Inheritance and the "Is a" Relationship

::: columns
:::: {.column width=50%}
::: {.block}
## "is a" relationship
Exists when one object is a specialized version of another object

  - Specialized object has all the characteristics of the general object
  - Rectangle is a Shape, Daisy is a Flower
:::

\tiny
For example, need to create classes for cars, trucks and SUVS

- All are automobiles
  - \tiny make, year, model, mileage, and price
  - These can be attributes for the base class
- In addition
  - \tiny Car has a number of doors
  - Pickup truck has a drive type
  - SUV has a passenger capacity
::::
:::: {.column width=50%}
- **Inheritance**: used to create an "is a" relationship between classes
- **Superclass** (base class, parent class): a (more) general class
- **Subclass** (derived class, child class): a specialized class
  - Extends the superclass
    - Inherits attributes and methods of the superclass
    - New attributes and methods can be added

\vspace{0.1in}
\tiny
- To indicate inheritance, the superclass name is placed in parentheses after subclass name
  - `class Car(Automobile)`
- The initializer method of a subclass calls the initializer method of the superclass and then
  initializes unique data attributes
- Add method definitions for unique methods
::::
:::

